       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A 1,600 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the analgesic benefit doesn't increase.\n\nHere are some doses I can enter instead:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day). This may be what was meant, since 1,600 mg is a common total daily dose.\n\nIf you meant 1,600 mg/day in total, tell me the per-dose amount and frequency and I'll enter it. If you want more analgesia than the maximum dose gives, I can enter a scheduled acetaminophen order as an adjunct, within its own daily limit. Which would you like?"
      }
